<title>USA: Virginia Surry nuke cuts power to shutdown - NRC.</title>
<headline>Virginia Surry nuke cuts power to shutdown - NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virginia Power Co's 781 megawatt Surry nuclear power unit 2 in Gravel Neck, Va. was reducing power early Tuesday ahead of a shutdown, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The unit was operating at 75 percent of capacity and was &quot;ramping down to shutdown,&quot; according to the NRC's daily plant status report Tuesday.</p>
<p>No reason was given for the shutdown. A company spokesman was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Virginia Power is a subsidiary of Dominion Resources Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
